            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "The suggested approach to inserting a character verbatim (without 'mini.pairs' \"rules\") is [to press `<C-v>`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0420076298c4457f200c2de468f65d080597a347/doc/mini-pairs.txt#L22) before it. So in this case it is `\"` - `\\` - `<C-v>` - `\"`.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">The suggested approach to inserting a character verbatim (without 'mini.pairs' \"rules\") is <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0420076298c4457f200c2de468f65d080597a347/doc/mini-pairs.txt#L22\">to press <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-v&gt;</code></a> before it. So in this case it is <code class=\"notranslate\">\"</code> - <code class=\"notranslate\">\\</code> - <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-v&gt;</code> - <code class=\"notranslate\">\"</code>.</p>",
            "bodyText": "The suggested approach to inserting a character verbatim (without 'mini.pairs' \"rules\") is to press <C-v> before it. So in this case it is \" - \\ - <C-v> - \".",
