                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "Not with a config, I am afraid. The current behavior is [documented](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0de7ac99824a315b9ef37aba0161f70bdbb1e66b/doc/mini-pairs.txt#L274-L2770 and is well established.\r\n\r\nThe issue here is how to interpret a `neigh_pattern`: whether failing to match it should discard the whole \"closeopen\" action or just some part of it. The decision was made to make it work only on \"open\" part and try \"close\" part without doing the match. Mostly for (very small) performance reasons, but also taking into account that inserting the single character can always be done with `<C-v>`.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Not with a config, I am afraid. The current behavior is [documented](<a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0de7ac99824a315b9ef37aba0161f70bdbb1e66b/doc/mini-pairs.txt#L274-L2770\">https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0de7ac99824a315b9ef37aba0161f70bdbb1e66b/doc/mini-pairs.txt#L274-L2770</a> and is well established.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The issue here is how to interpret a <code class=\"notranslate\">neigh_pattern</code>: whether failing to match it should discard the whole \"closeopen\" action or just some part of it. The decision was made to make it work only on \"open\" part and try \"close\" part without doing the match. Mostly for (very small) performance reasons, but also taking into account that inserting the single character can always be done with <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-v&gt;</code>.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "Not with a config, I am afraid. The current behavior is [documented](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0de7ac99824a315b9ef37aba0161f70bdbb1e66b/doc/mini-pairs.txt#L274-L2770 and is well established.\nThe issue here is how to interpret a neigh_pattern: whether failing to match it should discard the whole \"closeopen\" action or just some part of it. The decision was made to make it work only on \"open\" part and try \"close\" part without doing the match. Mostly for (very small) performance reasons, but also taking into account that inserting the single character can always be done with <C-v>.",
